(* The built-in theory Target (ADR 0049) is consistent: each model, one
   per target, meets every axiom. Programs that use Target do not prove
   this again, so this is where it is proved. The file it checks is the
   one compiled into piac, src/irgen/Target.pia. `rmw_flags` (ADR 0052)
   differs between the targets, so it has no axiom, and nothing is
   proved of it here.
// RUN: piac --verify --trust-report %S/../../src/irgen/Target.pia | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: 0 trusted items
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'arm64_macos' meets the axiom 'Target.ptr_pow2'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'arm64_macos' meets the axiom 'Target.little'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'arm64_macos' meets the axiom 'Target.align_16'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'arm64_macos' meets the axiom 'Target.page_pow2'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'arm64_macos' meets the axiom 'Target.line_pow2'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'arm64_macos' meets the axiom 'Target.vector_min'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'x86_64_linux' meets the axiom 'Target.ptr_pow2'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'x86_64_linux' meets the axiom 'Target.little'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'x86_64_linux' meets the axiom 'Target.align_16'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'x86_64_linux' meets the axiom 'Target.page_pow2'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'x86_64_linux' meets the axiom 'Target.line_pow2'
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the model 'x86_64_linux' meets the axiom 'Target.vector_min'
// CHECK-NOT: rmw_flags
// CHECK: {{[0-9]+}} proved, 0 failed, 0 skipped
*)
